 "source": "Keys: the xpub and xprv of BIP32 test vector 1, chain m, and the refused keys of BIP32 test vector 5 (https://github.com/bitcoin/bips/blob/master/bip-0032.mediawiki, BSD-2-Clause). BIP32 has no testnet vectors: the tpub and tprv are the vector 1 payload re-encoded with the testnet versions 0x043587CF and 0x04358394 and a recomputed checksum, and the WIFs are vector 1's chain-m private key (checked in TestTestnetVectorsDerived and TestWIFDerived). All are public test data, used only to test the refusal. Regtest vectors: the external wpkh and tr descriptors (with checksum, as listdescriptors prints them) of a throwaway Bitcoin Core 32.1 regtest wallet created by qualify TestOnchainSetup; a snapshot of one run, public data only (no private key leaves bitcoind).",
